2 TITL Research Records of Peter Craig
1 NOTE plantageägare i Pennsylvanien USA
1 NOTE Peter was born in New Sweden in 1647.  He was the son of Mats andElizabeth Hanson.  His father died and Elizabeth married Anders LarssonDalbo.  Peter was one of the first reps. to the General Assembly electedfrom the Fourth Tenth 
2 CONC (Glouchester Co. N.J.) in May 1685 and again in1687. He was a member of the House of Representatives, along with JohnRambo and Andrew Robeson, on May 1787 when they and the Governor, TheCouncil, and other members signed an agreeme
2 CONC nt to uphold to the utmost oftheir power, the authority of the King against all his enemies.  Peter'sfamily was devout, and several of the daughters married ministers who hadbeen sent from Sweden to serve the colonists and the con
2 CONC gregation ofGloria Dei Church at Wicaco.  See New Jersey Colonial Documents byWilliam Whitehead, Vols. 1 & 2.  His father may have been Matts Mattsoninstead.
2 CONT
2 CONT Facts about this person:
2 CONT
2 CONT Alt. Born 1647
2 CONT New Sweden (later Philadelphia,  PA)
2 CONT
