1 OCCU Ogift kapten
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HANS AUGUST PAULUS OLIVECRONA
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans was born 4 August 1806 at Mussvik and during childhood studied at home with brother Carl Adolf. He studied at Uppsala 1820-1822 and then became Ships boy on exercise corvette "Svalan" in 1822. A year later, 1823 he was still 
2 CONC on the "Svalan" but he had become a sea cadet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Below is a list of the Ships he served on during the next twenty years.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1824 "Experiment" - schooner- Capt. Freidenfelt
2 CONT
2 CONT 1825 "Suridice" - frigate - Capt. Loqueberg
2 CONT
2 CONT 1826 2nd lieutenant (11 May 1826) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1826  "Florida" - American merchant ship Stockholm - New York "Joka" - New York - Liguna di Madre - Antwerp - New York
2 CONT
2 CONT "Gevalia" - New York - Richmond - Bremen - Lisbon
2 CONT
2 CONT  1827 "Amphihite" - Lisbon - Helsingor  "Jean Baptiste" - Helsingor - Hull 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Antwerpen" Packete - Hull - Antwerp
2 CONT
2 CONT "Cerese" - Antwerp - Marseille
2 CONT
2 CONT "Hope" - Harseille - Celle - Philadelphia
2 CONT
2 CONT  1829 "Columbia"- New York - London "Neptunus" - London - Gotberg
2 CONT
2 CONT  1830-1834 "Chapman" - Stockholm - Rio de Janiero - Capt. Loqueberg  1834- 1835  "North Star" - Capt. Harcourt  "Spastiate"- Stockholm- Rio de Janiero- Buenos Aires- Bahia- Peruambucco - England
2 CONT
2 CONT  1835 Appointed member of commission for examining the rigging on "Brostroms Larobok" 1836 "Fadsueslaudit" - Capt.Melander
2 CONT
2 CONT 1837 "Jarramas" - Capt. Virqui
2 CONT
2 CONT 1838 "Josephine" - Capt. Nordenskjold
2 CONT
2 CONT 1840 1st lieutenant
2 CONT
2 CONT 1846 Lieutenant 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1851 Manager Swedish sea. chart office Stockholm
2 CONT
2 CONT On 28 November 1855 Hans became a Captain and it was around this time that he had a relationship with Charlotta Löfqvist (we still are not sure that this was her name) and had a son who was named Carl Johan (Born 26 October 1854).
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans was made R.S.O (Knight of the Order of the Sword) on 28 November 1859 and before he died on died 13 July 1860 at Ems in Germany he asked his bother Knut to look after his natural son Carl.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.igrin.co.nz/~hotchoc/HAPolive.htm
