1 NOTE Britta Rambo most likely came to America on one of the voyages prior tothe "Swan" which arrived in January 1648.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died sometime between July 8, 1684 when she consented to sale of landat Passyunk, and 1688 when her name was not listed as a co-grantor withPeter on a land deed dated that year.  She probably was buried at thechurchyard at Wic
2 CONC aco
2 CONT
2 CONT In a letter written in 1693 by Peter Gunnarson to his sister in Sweden,he stated that Britta was from Vasa in Sweden.  See Document File -- veryinteresting letter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mattzdotter is an alternate spelling for Mattsdotter.
