2 CONT ===Corrected Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/discussions/236854?msg=1500388 - https://www.geni.com/people/Cynthia-Forde/6000000026661666903 writes on 6 September 2021:
2 CONT
2 CONT >Ronald S. BEATTY, author of the Rambo Family Tree Vo. 1-5, and I are the genealogists for the Swedish Colonial Society. We have thoroughly researched the ancestors of [https://www.geni.com/people/Peter-Rambo/6000000005600906019?t
2 CONC hrough=6000000000077294699 Peter Gunnarsson Rambo] born 1612 . His father was likely Gunnar . Peters surname was not chosen until he was in New Sweden. Someone with a huge imagination created [https://www.geni.com/people/Gunnar-Ra
2 CONC mbo/6000000000077294699?through=6000000005600906019 Gunnar Mattson Rambo].
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT See
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Gunnarsson_Rambo Peter Gunnarsson Rambo english Wikipedia article]
2 CONT * [http://sites.google.com/site/rambofamilytree/ Rambo Family Tree]
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Gunnarsson chose the distinctive surname of Rambo from his place of origin, Hisingen, the northwestern section of Gothenburg, which is dominated by Ramberget (meaning, raven's mountain) with its enchanting view of the Gothen
2 CONC burg harbor. The correct adress In Sweden: Lundby, Rambergsstaden, Hisingen, Göteborgs Stad, Västra Götalands län, Västergötland, Sverige.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in 1612, Peter Rambo was 27 years old when he sailed to New Sweden as a laborer on the second voyage of the Kalmar Nyckel in 1639-40. After becoming a freeman, Peter married Brita Matsdotter from Vasa, Finland, on April 7, 16
2 CONC 47. Initially they lived in Kingsessing, but moved by 1669 to Passyunk on the northeast side of the Schuylkill ††.
2 CONT
2 CONT †† see an early map with two Rambo men on it: http://pagenealogy.net/maps/PA%20-%20John%20Thornton%20-%201681.jpg 
2 CONT
2 CONT During Governor Rising's rule (1654-55), Peter Rambo served on the Governor's Council. He continued to serve as a justice at New Amstel (the future New Castle, Delaware) under both Dutch rule (starting in 1658) and then under Engl
2 CONC ish rule (1664-80).
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Rambo had a prosperous farm, which included apple trees grown from seeds he had brought from Sweden. The "Rambo Apple"' is still grown in several of the northeastern states.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Rambo's hospitality was well known. Not only was the court occasionally held at his house, but it was also a place where many visitors were welcomed, notable among them William Penn, founder of Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter's wife of over 46 years, Brita Matsdotter, died at their Passyunk plantation on October 12, 1693. Peter Rambo was buried at the Swedes' log church at Wicaco on January 29, 1698, at the age of 85 years and almost eight months
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a letter written by Peter Rambo to his sister in Gothenburg in 1693, he had four sons and four daughters. One daughter died at the age of eight. Another daughter (married in 1693 but dead by August 3, 1694, when Peter
2 CONC  Rambo revised his will) has not been identified. The six surviving children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Gunnar Rambo''', born January 6, 1649, died January 1724 at the age of 75 at "Matzong" in Upper Merion township of present Montgomery County, Pa. Married''' Anna Cock''' (daughter of Peter Cock); nine children.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Gertrude Rambo''', born October 19, 1650, died after 1705 in Moyamensing (South Philadelphia). Married on November 22, 1668, to '''Anders Bengtsson''' (Andrew Bankson), who drowned in the Delaware River on September 14, 1705;
2 CONC  nine children.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Peter Rambo, Jr.''', born June 17, 1653, died December 12, 1729, in his 77th year in Lower Dublin township, Philadelphia County. Married on November 12, 1676, '''Magdalena Skute''' (daughter of Captain Sven Skute); seven chil
2 CONC dren.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Catharine Rambo''', born c. 1655, died after 1708 on Little Mantua Creek, Gloucester County, NJ. Married on February 16, 1674, '''Peter Mattsson''' (1647-1699), son of Matthias and Elizabeth Hansson and stepson of Anders Dalb
2 CONC o; nine children, including a daughter Elizabeth (1678-1736) who married the Rev. Andreas Rudman and a daughter Maria (1682-1739) who married the Rev. Andreas Sandel and died in Sweden, where her grandson, Baron John August Sandel
2 CONC s (1764-1831), later became a famous general.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Anders (Andrew) Rambo''', born 1658, died in 1698 at Passyunk (South Philadelphia). Married c. 1684''' Maria (daughter of Peter Cock)'''; six children.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''John Rambo''', born 1661, buried October 17,1741, in Gloucester County, N.J. Married '''Brigitta (daughter of Peter Cock)'''; 11 children.
2 CONT
