1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gunnar Rambo, born January 6, 1649, died January 1724 at the age of 75 at "Matzong" in Upper Merion township of present Montgomery County, Pa. Married Anna Cock (daughter of Peter Cock); nine children.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/33003184/gunnar-rambo
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunnar Mattson was the '''Ancestor of'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunnar Rambo, born January 6, 1649, died January 1724 at the age of 75 at "Matzong" in Upper Merion township of present Montgomery County, Pa. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Anna Cock (daughter of Peter Cock)
2 CONT
2 CONT Had nine children. Details:
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  GUNNAR RAMBO, Peter's eldest son, was born 6 Jan 1648/49 and married ANNEKA COCK in 1670.  Anneka was born about 1652, a daughter of Peter Larsson and Margaret (Lom) Cock and a sister of Maria and Brigitta Cock who married Gun
2 CONC nar's younger brothers Anders [#5] and John [#6].  (The Cock family is given at the end of this chapter.)  Gunnar Rambo was a large land owner and occupied a prominent place in the affairs of the province.  He was a member of the 
2 CONC first grand jury under William Penn, a peacemaker for Philadelphia County in 1684, and a member of the Pennsylvania Provincial Assembly in 1685.  Gunnar and his family belonged to Gloria Dei church at Wicaco, and in 1684 he and hi
2 CONC s brother Peter Jr. [#3] made a voluntary contribution of 30 guilders for the support of Rev. Jacob Fabritius.  The 1697-98 roll of the Swedes on the Delaware prepared by Andreas Rudman [#42], pastor of the Gloria Dei Church, list
2 CONC ed eight of the nine children in the family and their ages.  Gunnar Rambo died in Upper Merion Township in January 1724 at the age of 75.  His wife predeceased him.  Gunnar and Anna had the following children:
2 CONT * 	11.  JOHN RAMBO, Jr., b. ca 1673, d. ca 1746, m. 1) Anna Laicon, 2) Sarah (?)
2 CONT * 	12.  PETER RAMBO, b. ca 1678, d. Jul 1753, m. ?
2 CONT * 	13.  GUNNAR RAMBO, b. ca 1680, d. 1717-1724, unmarried
2 CONT * 	14.  ANDERS RAMBO, b. ca 1682, d. 3 Jul 1755 unmarried
2 CONT * 	15.  MNS RAMBO, b. ca 1684, d. Apr 1760, m. Catharina Boon
2 CONT * 	16.  BRIGITTA RAMBO, b. ca 1685, m. Matthias Holstein
2 CONT * 	17.  GABRIEL RAMBO, b. ca 1687, d. ca Nov 1734, m. Christian (?)
2 CONT * 	18.  MATTHIAS RAMBO, b. ca 1690, d. before 1724
2 CONT * 	19.  ELIAS RAMBO, b. ca 1693, will proved 1 Oct 1750, m. Maria Van Culen
2 CONT
2 CONT The  RAMBO FAMILY TREE Preliminary CD.  19 October 2011 Five Volumes: Descendants of Peter Gunnar Rambo  [http://sites.google.com/site/rambofamilytree On the web] and available on CD  By Beverly Nelson Rambo and Ronald Stephen Bea
2 CONC tty.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT #5. Gunnar Rambo (Shackamaxon, Northern Liberties, f 100): Gunnar, born in January 1649, was the eldest of the four Rambo brothers. He, too, married a daughter of Peter Larsson Cock - Anna Cock, born c. 1652. Their eldest son, Joh
2 CONC n Rambo, apparently was hired out to another family. Children then living at home were Peter (born 1678), Gunnar (1680), Anders (1682), MAns (1684), Brigitta (1685), Gabriel (1687) and Matthias (1690). As a resident of Shackamaxon
2 CONC , Gunnar served on the Pennsylvania Assembly in 1685. He sold his Shackamaxon plantation in 1697 and moved, with his son John, to Matsunk on the Schuylkill in Upper Merion township. Gumar died there in January 1724 at the age of 7
2 CONC 5. His wife predeceased him.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT of Matzon, Upper Merion
2 CONT
2 CONT • Gunnar Rambo was a member of the first grand jury underr WIlliam Penn's Govt. (1684). He was a member of the PA Assembly (1685 Pa Archives 2nd series Vol IX p.732
2 CONT
2 CONT • moved to Merion with his brother,Peter Jr. THeir lands joined.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Old Swedes built on this old tract (bought from Ezekiel, his son)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref. See THe Rambo Family of Philadelphia and Mointgomery Counties Pa (M.E. Wood in Collection of Genealogical Society of PA pp/ 4-13, 14-24, 25, 28,29
2 CONT --------------------
