2 CONT Married Anders Bengtsson on November 22, 1668. She was born in Kingsessing, New Sweden, Pennsylvania. The family lived in Moyamensing, along the Delaware River in present day South Philadelphia. Daughter of Peter Gunnarsson Rambo 
2 CONC and Brita Matsdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Anders Bengtsson was born in 1640 in Fåxarn parish [now Fuxerna parish] northeast of Gothenburg, Sweden and sailed to New Sweden on the ship Mercurius in 1656. Anders was a large land owner in New Sweden, wrote his own name as An
2 CONC dreas Bengtsson, and was known in the English records as Andrew Bankson. The family lived in Moyamensing, along the Delaware River in present South Philadelphia. Andreas was a church warden, trustee and lay reader of the Wicaco ch
2 CONC urch and contributed faithfully to the support of the clergy. Anders Bengtsson was also politically active, serving as a justice on the New Court at Upland 1681-82, 1693 and 1701-03 and being elected to the Pennsylvania Assembly i
2 CONC n 1683, 1686 and 1698. As a member of the Assembly, he witnessed the charter of Pennsylvania on 2 Apr 1683 and was personally known by William Penn.       By the time of his death in 1705, he owned substantial property south of Ph
2 CONC iladelphia in Moyamensing and Passyunk townships and "five hundred acres in the Swedes' tract at Manatawny [Amity Township, present Berks County], patented to him on 11 June 1705 (Phila. Exemplification Book 1:636-637; Patents, A-
2 CONC 3:209). This land [in Manatawny] was sold by his sons to John Oakley on 13 Oct. 1707. (Phila. deeds)".1 Anders Bengtsson drowned in the Delaware River and was buried at Gloria Dei Church (Wicaco) on 14 Sep 1705. His wife survived 
2 CONC him. (Dr. Peter Stebbins Craig wrote a biography and a chronology of Anders Bankston and family which are included in Appendix 5.) _____________________________________________Marriage 1 Anders* or Andreas Bengtsson Bankson b: 164
2 CONC 0 in Hanstrom farm, Faxarn (today Fuxerna parish), Alvsborg lan, northeast of Gothenburg, SwedenMarried: 22 NOV 1668 in Philadelphia Co., PA ---------------------
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 1. Bengt Andersson Bengtsson born 1669 in Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania2. Anders Bengtsson (Bankson), Jr.* born 1672 in Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania3. Peter Bengtsson born 6 March 1677 in Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania
2 CONC 4. Catharine Bengtsson born 29 January 1679 in Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania5. John B. Bengtsson, Sr. born 31 March 1681 in Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania6. Jacob Bengtsson born 19 October 1684 in Philadelphia County, Penns
2 CONC ylvania7. Briggitta Bengtsson born 10 April 1687 in Philadelphia (Montgomery County), Pennsylvania8. Daniel Bengtsson, Sr. born 22 January 1691 in Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania9. Joseph Bengtsson, Sr. born 2 March 1696 in Phil
2 CONC adelphia County, Pennsylvania
