1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The biographical profile of the unknown Miss Rambo—the first wife of Andrew "Anders" Nilsson Friend and the mother of Israel Nilsson Friend—is a fascinating puzzle in early American genealogy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Because her personal name was never transcribed into surviving colonial documents, historians and the Swedish Colonial Society have reconstructed her factual profile entirely through the legal records of her male relatives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile Summary
2 CONT Birth: Circa 1663–1665 in the New Sweden Colony (along the Delaware River, modern-day Pennsylvania).
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: Before August 1694.Parents: Daughter of the famous Swedish founder Peter Gunnarsson Rambo (1612–1698) and Britta Mattsdotter (c. 1630–1693).
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Married Andrew "Anders" Nilsson Friend circa 1685–1689 in the Delaware River valley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Documented Children: Her primary surviving child was the Indian trader and diplomat Israel Nilsson Friend (born c. 1690–1693).
2 CONT
2 CONT Factual Documentation & Evidence
2 CONT Her existence is proven by intersecting historical pieces of evidence compiled by premier New Sweden historian Dr. Peter Stebbins Craig:
2 CONT 1. The 1693 Peter Rambo LetterIn a famous letter written on May 30, 1693, by the aging patriarch Peter Gunnarsson Rambo to his sister back in Gothenburg, Sweden, he explicitly boasted that he had three living daughters who were ma
2 CONC rried with children.
2 CONT 2. The 1694 Rambo Will (The Death Proof)Just over a year later, on August 3, 1694, Peter Rambo rewrote his Last Will and Testament. In this final version, only two of his daughters (Gertrude and Catherine) are named. The third unn
2 CONC amed daughter mentioned in his 1693 letter had passed away in the interim, pinning her death to roughly late 1693 or early 1694.
2 CONT 3. The 1740 John Rambo Court Affidavit (The Ultimate Link)The absolute proof connecting her to the Friend family comes from a 1740 legal affidavit signed by her brother, John Rambo.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Rambo traveled westward to the frontier of Maryland to visit Andrew Friend.In the official court document detailing the trip, John Rambo explicitly refers to Andrew Friend as his "brother" (the 18th-century legal term commonl
2 CONC y used for a brother-in-law).Because John's sisters Gertrude and Catherine were married to other men, the only possible way for Andrew Friend to be John Rambo's brother-in-law was if Andrew had been married to the deceased third R
2 CONC ambo sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT Evolution of the Research: The Israel Helm ErrorIf you dive deep into older family history books, you will find a major contradiction that often confuses family tree builders:The Old Theory (1991): Dr. Craig initially published a 
2 CONC theory that Anders Friend's first wife was an unnamed daughter of Captain Israel Helm, based on the fact that Anders named his eldest son "Israel".
2 CONT
2 CONT The Modern Correction (2005): Following the discovery and cross-referencing of the 1740 John Rambo affidavit and the 1694 Rambo estate distributions, Dr. Craig officially corrected the record. It was definitively ruled that she wa
2 CONC s a Rambo. The name "Israel" was likely given to her son to honor Israel Helm Jr., who was Anders Friend's closest childhood friend and neighbor before disappearing at sea.
2 CONT
2 CONT —-
2 CONT According to a letter written by Peter Rambo to his sister in Gothenburg in 1693, he had four sons and four daughters. One daughter died at the age of eight. Another daughter (married in 1693 but dead by August 3, 1694, when Peter
2 CONC  Rambo revised his will) has not been identified.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference: MyHeritage Family Trees - SmartCopy: Dec 26 2019, 5:34:11 UTC
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a letter written by Peter Rambo to his sister in Gothenburg in 1693, he had four sons and four daughters. One daughter died at the age of eight. Another daughter (married in 1693 but dead by August 3, 1694, when Peter
2 CONC  Rambo revised his will) has not been identified.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Rambo-556
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Daughter RAMBO, name not known, is believed to have married ANDERS NILSSON FRIEND who born about 1656, son of Nils Larsson FrÑnde and Anna Andersdotter. In the 1693 census Andrew was listed with four in his household (himself, 
2 CONC his wife and two children). The family lived in Ridley Township, Chester Co., PA until about 1694 when he moved to New Castle Co., Delaware to live on Andrew's 200-acres of his father's land located between Brandywine Creek and Re
2 CONC d Clay Creek. The Rambo daughter died between May 1693 and August 1694, the dates her father, Peter Gunnarson Rambo, wrote his sister in Sweden and made his will. Anders Friend remarried to Isabel by 24 Jun 1699 when they were ass
2 CONC igned pews in the new Holy Trinity Church at Christina [now Wilmington]. They moved by 1710 to Cecil County, Maryland where he was host to Rev. Andreas Sandel [#44] when the latter attended the wedding of Jonas AurÇn and Lydia Jus
2 CONC tis. From there they moved again west to the mouth of the Conococheague with his youngest son, Charles Friend. In 1740 he was living with his son Israel near Harper's Ferry, Virginia. Andrew died in 1748 at the home of his son Cha
2 CONC rles on the Potomac River. His Bible inspired an article by Peter Craig, "The Odyssey of Andrew Friend's Swedish Bible" in the Swedish American Genealogist, vol. 16 (Mar 1996). A great deal more about Anders Nilsson Friend is incl
2 CONC uded in a paper by Peter Craig, The Family of Nils Larsson FrÑnde (Friend), 1988.
2 CONT
2 CONT It seems likely that this first child of Anders Nilsson Friend was a child of his first wife, presumed Rambo. It is also possible that Anders Friend married a daughter of Israel Helm as a second wife immediately after the death of
2 CONC  his first wife. 71. ISRAEL FRIEND, will dated 12 Aug 1749 names wife Sarah and children: Jonas, Jacob, Charles, Catharine and Mary. It is not known whether either of the other known children of Anders Friend were children of his 
2 CONC first wife. Those children are: 72. CHARLES FRIEND, will proved 20 March 1751 73. MARY FRIEND, m. Robert Turner 3 May 1727 in Northeast, Maryland.
