1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bonde i Ostvik. Ägare 1564-1592 i Östanbäck 10, Skellefteå lfs
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ägde Östanbäck 10 åren 1564-1592. Köpman,skräddare,Birkarl,kyrkvärd och sexman
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ägare 1564-92 i Östanbäck 10, Skellefteå lfs (AC) (Ulf Lundström)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Kallas Nils Hansson i Ostvik. Bonde, birlkarl, köpman, nämndeman, men själv dömd ( se källorna) Ägare 1564-1592 av Östanbäck 10 Källor: https://familjenbostrom.se/genealogi/anor/leif/11-301_1977.htm https://lokalhistoriaskelleftea
2 CONC .se/pdf/Skelleftebygden/2018-2.pdf https://www.genvagar.nu/show.asp?PersonId=281058 http://raggragg.duckdns.org/anor/mis/pfa1fe71d.html
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT From Ulfström (cited by Sikeborg): "From printed works, Ulf Lundström states in his book about Skellefteå's older settlements during the Vasa era that the village of Ostvik was divided by a stream, something that created a natural
2 CONC  division of the village into "Västanbäcken" and "Östanbäcken". The eastern side eventually came to be written as a separate village, while the name Ostvik came to be reserved for the western part. The tax home in Östanbäck, which
2 CONC  later gets land register number ten, was managed in the years 1564–1594 by Nils Hansson. According to Lundström, Nils Hansson/tailor was the son of the previous farmer on the homestead Hans Mårtensson, but no evidence is provided
2 CONC . If the relationship is based only on the name change Hans/Hansson, all that can be said is that this relationship is possible, given that these names are among the most common. . . . However, it is not clear from the report . . 
2 CONC . that he lived in Ostvik."
2 CONT
2 CONT From Kråken: "Nils Hansson owns the farm from 1564-1592. According to Johan Bure, he is married to Mariet Larsdotter, daughter of Lars Andersson in Yttervik and his wife Anna Mosesdotter from Bureå. . . . Nils Hansson was a mercha
2 CONC nt 1556-1566 and 1586-1590. In 1556 he was called Nils Skräddare and then paid 3 marks in merchant's money (köpmanspengar). . . . In 1590, Nils Hansson is both a merchant (landsköpman) and a birkarl (one who had right to trade wit
2 CONC h the Sami people). He pays 8 marks as a birkarl and 5 marks as a merchant. Nils Hansson is a nämndeman (grand juror) during the period 1569-1587. In 1584 he is a church orderly (sexman) and church warden (kyrkvärd).
2 CONT
2 CONT From Genvagar: "In 1547, he was fined 3 marks for a double lien. In 1553, he was fined 1.5 marks to the bishop for lying in bed. At the summer parliament in 1554, he was fined 5 marks for defamation. At the Winter Parliament in 15
2 CONC 58, he was fined 40 marks for disobedience (olydnad) in connection with land purchases, he gave 4 marks. Älvsborgslösen in 1571, he had 62 lods of silver, 90 marks in money, 1.5 bowl pounds of tin, 2 bowl pounds of copper, 12 cows
2 CONC , 1 steer aged 2 years, 1 heifer aged 1 year, 10 sheep, 10 goats and goats and 2 horses worth 23 mark. The property was valued at 539 marks and 6 öre. In 1586, he helped build a galley (galeja) for the crown in Kåge."
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT https://www.genvagar.nu/show.asp?PersonId=281058
2 CONT Kråken 24 database, https://kråken.se/ person 558333.
2 CONT Urban Sikeborg, "Johan Bures släktbok" USB (2017), person ID 558333 gives sources "Bure/s154/92" (birth) and "SK1" (death); biography in notes.
2 CONT Ulf Lundström, "Skellefteå socken 1650-1790," (1997), pp. 70,82.
2 CONT Ulf Lundström, "Bönder och gårdar i Skellefteå socken 1539-1650" (2004), p. 85, Östanbäck 10
