1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Reference: https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/6989691/person/-1185732219/facts
2 CONT *https://www.wikitree.com/index.php?title=Bengtsson-569&errcode=saved
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Bankston, Sr. (Andreas Bengtsson) drowned in the Schuylkill River in 1706. Andrew, Jr. (1672-1759) was married to a Gertrude Boore. Andrew, Jr. died in Chester PA (this is a few miles SW of Philadelphia on the Delaware Rive
2 CONC r). Andrew, Jr and Gertrude's children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew III b.1696
2 CONT Elizabeth b.1698
2 CONT Peter
2 CONT Daniel
2 CONT Lawrence b.1704 Chester PA d.1774 Guilford County NC
2 CONT Andrew Bankson Jr. was born 1672 to Anders Bengtsson and Gertrude Rambo, probably in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Bankson Jr. married Gertrude Lars Boore about 1695, mostly certainly in Gloria Dei. According to the vestry records of Gloria Dei 1696–1699 by The Rev. Rudman, there were four members of the family living above the church i
2 CONC n the division of Pasquesting at the time of his father, Anders Bengtsson's death in 1706.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Bankson Jr. was living Passayunk in 1706 when he received an inheritance from his father, Anders Bengtsson. He was called a yeoman and was recorded as working on a ship. In 1706, he was made one of the executors of his fath
2 CONC er's will.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Bankson Jr. died sometime after he executed a deed in 1746 in Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT Andrew Bankson's death was recorded in Philadelphia Monthly Meeting in Pennsylvania. He died on 06 Seventh 1759, translating to 6 July 1759.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT National Society of the Sons of the American Revolution
2 CONT The application for SAR membership #80281 was submitted on February 18, 1959. The application stated that Andrew Bankston was born in 1672 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania and died in 1750 in Chester, Pennsylvania. His parents were A
2 CONC ndrew Bankston and Gartrude Rambo. His wife was Gertrude, and his son was Lawrence Bankston.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 Forde, Cynthia V, and Anne C. Terry. The Spirit in the South: Stories of Our Grandmothers' Spirit : Bankston, Brooks, Cobb, Henderson, Herndon, Irvin, Jarrett, Lea, Martin, Mathis, Mcdonald, Miller, Rambo, Sappin
2 CONC gton, Weaver. Bloomington, Ind: AuthorHouse, 2009. Print. Page 112.
2 CONT ↑ Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy Vol. II, Ancestry.com. U.S., Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy, Vol I–VI, 1607-1943 [database on-line]. Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations, Inc., 2013.
2 CONT ↑ Ancestry.com. U.S., Sons of the American Revolution Membership Applications, 1889-1970 [database on-line]. Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations, Inc., 2011. Original data: Sons of the American Revolution Membership Applicatio
2 CONC ns, 1889-1970. Louisville, Kentucky: National Society of the Sons of the American Revolution. Microfilm, 508 rolls.
