2 CONT 1793 Deposition of James Lea About 47 years ago he married in the family of Laurance Banckston senior and he was well acquainted with the proceedings of the family as one might be in that case. The depondant also sayeth that he of
2 CONC ten heard Laurance Banckston sayeth that he held a claim of land lying on the south side of a tract of a larger tract of land where he was now residing lying on the waters of Panther Creek now in Caswell County. The depondent furt
2 CONC her sayeth that he don’t know that ever the said Banckston obtained any right to the said land.The depondant further sayeth that the said Banckston he believes died in Anson County before the War and further sayeth that he never k
2 CONC new of any will that the said Banckston made. And the depondant further sayeth that Andrew Bankston was the eldest son of saidLaurance, he believes the heir at law and that Peter Bankston was the second son of said Laurance, and L
2 CONC aurance Bankston was the third son of the said Laurance Senr. That Daniel Bankston was the fourth son of the said Laurance and Jacob Bankston was the fifth son of the said Laurance and the youngest son.
