1 NOTE In 1711 Peter Rambo, Jr. conveyed a parcel of 80 acres to his oldest son,Swan.  Swan later owned a plantation of 400 acres in Chester Co. whichbecame Lancaster Co.  He also owned the Swedish Bible which was printedin Stoclholm in 
2 CONC 1703.  The names of the children were listed in it, andit was passed on to his oldest son Peter.  Swan later married Barbara.When he died, his estate inventory included the following: 3 horses, 4cows, 1 calf, a parcell of hogs, a 
2 CONC Negro wench aged 8 years, varioustools, a parcel of books and household goods.
