2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Nilsson "Anders" Friend (Frände)
2 CONT Lifespan:
2 CONT Born circa 1659 at Upland (now Chester/Delaware County, Pennsylvania)
2 CONT
2 CONT The parents of Andrew "Anders" Nilsson Friend are fully documented as Nils Larsson Frände (Friend) and Anna Andersdotter.Because they were primary founders of the New Sweden colony along the Delaware River, their family history is
2 CONC  meticulously preserved in early colonial court documents, land deeds, and the research archives of the Swedish Colonial Society.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died circa 1740–1741 near Harper's Ferry, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical Profile: Anders was a noted frontier trader, interpreter, and ranger who lived among Native American tribes along the Susquehanna and Potomac rivers. His use of the patronymic naming system (Nilsson, meaning "son of Nil
2 CONC s") explains why his son Israel carried the middle name "Nilsson".
2 CONT Spouse: Unknown Rambo (First Wife), daughter of Peter Gunnarsson Rambo
2 CONT The Record: Extensive research from historians like Dr. Peter Stebbins Craig (author of The 1693 Census of the Swedes on the Delaware) and archived genealogies via WikiTree confirm that Israel Friend was born to Anders’ unnamed fi
2 CONC rst wife, who was a daughter of the prominent Rambo family.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: Many automated tree databases on Find a Grave or FamilySearch mistakenly list Anders' second wife, Isabela Helm (or Stidham), as Israel’s biological mother. However, primary colonial court distributions and age timelines est
2 CONC ablish that Israel was born during Anders’ first marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT —-
2 CONT
2 CONT '''https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Friend-184
2 CONT '''Andrew Nilsson “Anders” Friend BIRTH	1659 Chester, Delaware County, Pennsylvania, USA DEATH	1741 (aged 81–82) Williamsport, Washington County, Maryland, USA BURIAL	 Friend's Family Cemetery Williamsport, Washington County, Mary
2 CONC land, 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/133817153/andrew-nilsson-friend
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Mary Friend Turner
2 CONT
2 CONT Israel F Friend 1693–1753
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Friend 1700–1756
2 CONT
2 CONT In September, 1686 Nils Lawson (Nicholas Friend) was named Constable of Chester Township, but in early December, 1686 he became gravely ill and his son Andrew took over as Constable on December 3, 1686.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders (Andrew) was to become the progenitor of the Ivydale, Clay Co., West Virginia "Friend" line and Anders' son Israel was named ambassador to the Indians by the governor of Maryland in 1725. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their second son, Johannes (John) was to be the progenitor of the Garrett Co. (formerly Allegany Co.) Maryland "Friend" line.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes' grandson John Lewis Friend Sr. was the first white settler to the Garrett Co. area in 1765. The land he purchased from local Indians eventually became the town of Friendsville. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT On 28 November 1732, Andrew Friend, age 75 years, came before the Court of Prince George’s County, Maryland. He told them he had no servants and no slaves and requested that he be made “levy free”. His request was granted (Prince 
2 CONC George’s County Court Records, Book 9, Liber 5, page 112. Colonial Records of the Upper Potomac, William H. Rice, 2010.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Friend's first wife (name unknown was the daughter of Peter Gunnarsson Rambo, not Israel Friend. This is shown by a 1740 affidavit by John Rambo, who visited is "brother" [brother-in-law] Anders Friend in western Maryland. 
2 CONC In a letter written to his sister in Gothenburg on 30 May 1693, Peter Rambo had mentioned three daughters who were then married with children. In his 1694 will, however, only two of these three daughters were still living. The dau
2 CONC ghter who had died must have been Andrew's first wife in order that the indicated relationship between Andrew Friend and John Rambo to be true.
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew's second wife's name was Isabela Helm.
2 CONT
2 CONT History found [http://books.google.com/books?id=5TwW25t42BEC&pg=SL5-PA9&lpg=SL5-PA9&dq=%22MANS+NILSSON+KLING%22&source=bl&ots=cI3AnKJQq1&sig=fwGtBiFJKIPuaT1Gpb3Q5H4eFZo&hl=en&sa=X&ei=BNXfU_OeDNDYigKblIH4AQ&ved=0CEcQ6AEwBw#v=onepag
2 CONC e&q=%22MANS%20NILSSON%20KLING%22&f=false here].
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional history found [http://http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=rene33&id=I4531 here].
