1 OCCU Indian trader and interpreter, Shawnee Ambassador, Trader, Settler, 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Chronological Biography
2 CONT 1693 Birth: Born at Upland (Ridley Township, Chester County, Pennsylvania) to Swedish colonist Anders Nilsson (Andrew Friend). His father was listed in the landmark 1693 Census of the Swedes on the Delaware.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1725 Commission: Appointed on July 25, 1725, by Governor Charles Calvert of Maryland to serve as an official Indian trader and ambassador to the Shawnee tribes.
2 CONT 1727 First Pioneer: Settled permanently along the upper Potomac River near the mouth of the Antietam Creek. Primary source logs indicate he was the only white settler living in this remote frontier area before 1732.
2 CONT 1734 Land Acquisition: Granted 300 acres of land on August 21, 1734, derived from an original 42,289-acre Virginia Colony patent issued by Lieutenant Governor William Gooch.
2 CONT 1736–1746 Exploration & Industry: Acted as a geographic guide for Lord Fairfax’s surveying parties mapping the Potomac River. He also initiated early regional iron ore mining operations.
2 CONT 1749 Death & Probate: Executed his Last Will and Testament on August 12, 1749. The will was processed in probate court shortly thereafter, confirming his death in the Shenandoah Valley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lineage and Family Record
2 CONT Grandfather: Captain Nils Larsson Frände (Kinsman), a prominent early immigrant to New Sweden who served as Constable of Chester Township.
2 CONT Parents: Anders Nilsson (Andrew) Friend and his first wife (a daughter of early settler Israel Helm).
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Sarah Catherine (often cited in genealogies as Sarah Bokavar).
2 CONT The five documented children of Israel Friend are explicitly named in his Last Will and Testament, which he signed on August 12, 1749.
2 CONT In his will, Israel directly identifies the birth order of his sons, followed by the legacies left to his daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT The Sons (Listed by birth order in the Will)
2 CONT -Jonas Friend (Eldest Son): Born circa 1725–1730. Formally designated in the will as the "eldest son," he inherited a primary tract of land. He later served in the French and Indian War and built the historic frontier stronghold k
2 CONC nown as Friend's Fort in the Tygart Valley (modern-day West Virginia).
2 CONT -Jacob Friend (Second Son): Born circa 1727–1731. Explicitly designated as the "second son," he was bequeathed the specific homestead and land where Israel was living at the time of his death.
2 CONT -Charles Friend (Youngest Son): Born circa 1733–1734. Explicitly designated as the "youngest son," he inherited 120 acres of land. Because he was still a minor when his father died, later 1761 court records formally list him as th
2 CONC e "orphan of Israel Friend" when choosing a legal guardian.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Daughters (Listed at the end of the Will)
2 CONT -Catherine Friend: Mentioned directly after the sons, she received a specific legacy and later married into the Peck family.
2 CONT -Mary Friend: Listed alongside her sister Catherine to receive her paternal legacy.
2 CONT
2 CONT —-
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Israel Friend 
2 CONT * BIRTH	1693 
2 CONT * DEATH	1753 (aged 59–60) 
2 CONT * BURIAL	 Friend's Family Cemetery Williamsport, Washington County, Maryland,
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LZP9-44W
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Friend-510
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/134531056/israel-f-friend
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonas Friend 1725–1807
2 CONT Jacob Friend 1727–1818
2 CONT
2 CONT Israel Friend House
2 CONT The Israel F. Friend house was built in 1737 and is located near Bakerton, West Virginia. The land was a gift to Israel from the Indian Chiefs of the Five Nations with an addition of a regal grant from the Governor of Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friend's land encompassed 1672 acres. After Israel's death the land became a mining  site for iron ore for the next 100 years. The land and site were owned by several people including President John Adams. The house was used durin
2 CONC g the Civil War as a military hospital. This picture was taken about,1988 and the land was owned at the time by Becky and Allen Sullivan who were restoring it. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Ref: Mary Ann St. Louis   6th Great Grandaughter of Israel Friend  LindaLabinoriginally submitted this to Labin-Mullenax Family Tree on 1 Jul 2009
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources claim that Israel Friend arranged for John Valentine House to marry Israel's wife Sarah Bokavar following his death, to protect her and his children's estate, since Indians were not allowed to own property.) Sarah Bokavar'
2 CONC s Second Husband 1700-1800 , DE, PA, MD, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Written by Linda L. Labin, PhD 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Bokavar Friend's Second Marriage?
2 CONT
2 CONT Some researchers have suggested that Sarah Bokavar, the wife of Israel Friend, was in fact an Indian (if so, probably a Shawnee, since these were the people who called Israel a "blood brother"). If true, then it is possible that c
2 CONC laims she remarried after Israel's death may have merit. While descendants apparently never made reference to Sarah as an Indian, the prejudice of the time would have dictated the necessity of concealing this fact. Of course, "pas
2 CONC sing for white" became easier as spouses were white, the descendants having a very diluted strain of Indian blood. It has therefore been suggested that John Valentine House married Sarah Bokavar Friend after Israel's death, at Isr
2 CONC ael's behest, in order to protect his property and estate. In those days, Indians were forbidden to own property, so even if Israel left everything to Sarah and their children, someone could have contested the will under the guise
2 CONC  of Sarah's Indian blood (and, thus, her children's) which would preclude them inheriting. It does make sense that Israel would provide for his family in this way, as the Friends had been ripped off before, when Lord Baltimore sto
2 CONC le land they had bought from the Shawnee. Of course, the alternative argument made by Dr. Peter S. Craig, is that, according to the original court documents, after Israel's death, Sarah and her children did in fact receive their i
2 CONC nheritance.
2 CONT
2 CONT In an archived discussion of burial sites and tombstones of the Moore family, speculation arose about John Valentine House's possible grave in the Moore cemetery: "to show possible reasons why John House might be buried in a Moore
2 CONC  family cemetery, ... Sarah Moore married John Harrod in Virginia about 1734. This Sarah Moore Harrod was the mother of James Harrod, founder of Harrodsburg, and of Nelly or Eleanor Harrod who married John Valentine House, and oth
2 CONC ers. Sarah Moore Harrod had a brother named Simeon Moore who died in Mercer Co in 1814. He had a son named Thomas Moore who died in Mercer Co. in 1835. A will recorded in Mercer Co. for this Thomas Moore names daughters Isabella B
2 CONC ingham, and Ann Worley, also a daughter named Polly Harrod who married John Harrod, a distant relative, in 1809. ...Thomas Moore, Sr. who died 1835, was the nephew of Sarah Moore Harrod and a first cousin of Eleanor House, whose h
2 CONC usband [was] John Valentine House.... They had the following children: 5 F iv. Nancy Eleanor HARROD-2591 born about 1734 in Lancaster, PA. She died about 1800 in KY.  
2 CONT
2 CONT "Eleanor Harrod, daughter of John Sr. and Sarah (Moore) Harrod, married John Valentine House, son of John House, who died in Frederick County, MD in 1752, and his wife, Susannah. Eleanor and John House lived in Frederick Co., VA i
2 CONC n the area that is now Berkeley Co., West Virginia. Further definite information about this family has not been found, but it is believed that the four men who lived near the Harrods on Ten Mile Creek, now Greene County, PA, were 
2 CONC their sons. They all had military service under Col. William Harrod, brother of Eleanor Harrod House. They were Levi, Samuel, John, and Andrew House. Thomas House.... ????-1795, John House...... ????-1799."
2 CONT
2 CONT "John Valentine HOUSE-5331, son of John Valentine HOUSE-238 and Susannah Margaret EDWARDS -239 (MRIN:200), in 1757 in Frederick Co, . MD. John was born 1720 in Baden, Alsace, Germany. He died 1808 in Nelson Co., KY. JVH married Sa
2 CONC rah Bokavar Friend by a prior arrangement with Israel Friend, her husband. This was immediately after the death of I. Friend, to protect her and her children and their property. Indians could not own property at that time. He was 
2 CONC an Indian trader/trapper on Upper Potomac before coming to KY. JVH was best friends with Nancy Eleanor's brother, James Harrod, the founder of Harrodsburg in 1774, the first town in Kentucky. John and Eleanor House lived for a num
2 CONC ber of years in the part of Frederick County which became Hampshire County. Poll for the election of George Washington the Virginia House of Burgesses, July 24, 1758, shows: John House - vote for Mr. West. John House - Vote for Ca
2 CONC pt. Swearingen.  In September 1758 he is listed as Sgt. John House in the Virginia Colonial Militia with brother-in-law William Harrod, in Bedford County, Virginia. John and his sons also appear in the 1776 petition against the st
2 CONC ate of Transylvania. In 1766 John with brothers George and William was a signer of the petition to Governor Horatio Sharpe calling for an assembly to pay bills to public creditors."   
2 CONT
2 CONT "In 1782 John and son John were in Hampshire County, Virginia, but John Sr. was gone by 1784. Mercer Co., KY--A list of Lands taken by Gabriel Slaughter, 1795--June 18 John House-135 acres second rate land-tax paid 1792-92. There 
2 CONC may be some confusion between which wife is the mother of John V.'s  children.  JVH, his brothers Samuel and Andrew had military service under Col. William Harrod, brother of Eleanor Harrod House."
2 CONT
2 CONT Another source repeats the story of John V. House marrying Sarah Bokavar:   Israel Friend, a son of Andrew and Isabela (Helm) Friend, was born in Delaware County PA before 1693 and died near Harper's Ferry VA in 1753. His will was
2 CONC  dated August 12, 1749 and names his children and his brother Charles. The will was probated in Frederick County MD June 5, 1753. His will is also recorded in Augusta County VA Will book 2, page 125. He married Sarah Bokavar. Sara
2 CONC h married John Valentine House after Israel died. Sarah died in Augusta County about 1764. Governor Calvert of MD commissioned Israel Friend as an Indian trader and ambassador to the Shawnee Indians on the Potomac River. The follo
2 CONC wing deed is recorded in the Fairfax VA museum and is made out to Israel Friend:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Whereas it be known to all manner of persons to whom it May concern that, we Cunnawchala, Taw Wenaw, Capt. Slvilite, Toile Hangee, Shoe Hays, Calakahahatt being Kings and Rulers of the five nations, for natural love and affection
2 CONC  we bear to our brother Israel Friend.We give unto him and heirs, executors, administrators and assigns a certain piece of land lying between the Potowmack River beginning at the mouth of Aucictum [Antietam] Creek at Cox Elders, m
2 CONC arked with three notches on every side and run up said river two hundred shoots as far as an arrow can be flung out of a bow and to be one hundred shoots right back from the river so containing its square until it intersects with 
2 CONC the said creek again with aforesaid land against the mouth of the creek which said land we said Indians and our heirs do warrant and forever defend unto the said Israel Friend, his heirs, executors, administrators, and assigns for
2 CONC ever with all the appurtenances thereunto belonging as fishing, fowling, hawking, hunting, and all other privileges thereunto belonging with paying unto some of us two ears of Indian corn for every year if demanded as witness our 
2 CONC hands and seals this tenth day of January one thousand seven hundred and twenty seven. Cunnawchala (his mark) Seal  Taw, Tenaw (his mark) Seal  Capt. Sivilite (his mark) Seal  Toile Hangee (his mark) Seal  Shoe Hays (his mark) Sea
2 CONC l  Calakahatt (his mark) Seal".  The deed was enrolled November 27, 1730. This land was on the Potomac River in Price George's County MD and later became the Civil War battlefield Antietam.
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1734, Israel had built a mill in Frederick County MD. By 1748, the mill was owned by Christian Orndorff. Israel was an iron worker and had a smelting furnace on Antietam Creek in MD. In 1734, he was mining iron ore on a tract o
2 CONC f land bordering the Potomac River in present-day Jefferson County WV. It is not known whether he had a furnace on this site or whether he took the ore to Antietam Creek for smelting. Israel cast a great number of bells, the fines
2 CONC t on the market and each bore his initials. He was on the rent rolls of Frederick County VA for 1746. He owned an estate called "Keep Trust" [Keep Tryst] on the VA side of the Potomac River nears Harper's Ferry VA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Israel and Sarah Friend:
2 CONT
2 CONT  * 40. (1). Jonas b.c. 1725 d.Nov 15 1807 m.Sarah Skidmore 1754
2 CONT *  41. (2). Jacob b.c. 1731. d. 1818 m.Elizabeth Skidmore Aug 19 1754
2 CONT *  42. (3). Charles b.c. 1734 d.Nov 1811 m.Rachel Tackett Sep 20 1783; m. Agnes Holly Aug 31 1794
2 CONT *  43. (4). Catherine b.c. 1736, Rockingham, VA.
2 CONT *  44. (5). Mary b.c. 1738.m.Jonathan Clark
2 CONT *  45. (6). James
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1744 John House was beginning to have land surveyed for himself near the mouth of Antietam Creek in present-day Washington County (MD) and here he also purchased a part of Israel Friend's "Antietam Bottom." John House purchased
2 CONC  a part of Israel Friend's "Antietam Bottom" in 1744.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Craig has identified the earliest American ancestor as Nils Larsson Frande, who came to New Jersey by 1650, as well as Nils Larsson Frande's wife, and their ten surviving children. Contrary to family legend, Gertrude, the gran
2 CONC dmother of Declaration of Independence signer John Morton, was not one of the daughters. The Garret Co., MD Friends descend from Nils' son Johannes Nilsson, or John Friend, as he came to be known. The Pendleton and Randolph County
2 CONC  branches of this family descend from Israel Friend, who died in Frederick Co, VA. Israel Friend was the son of Anders Nilsson Frande, or Andrew Friend, the oldest surviving son of Nils Larsson Frande. Copies of his manuscript can
2 CONC  be bought from Dr. Peter S. Craig; 3406 Macomb St., N.W.; Washington, D.C. 20016-3160.
2 CONT
2 CONT Additionally, in a Pension Claim for service in the Revolutionary War, Levi House presents evidence of service and indicates his parentage:  Levi House, son of [John] Valentine House and Sarah Catherine Bachoffen/Bokavar, was born
2 CONC  about 1754 in Ten Mill Creek, Frederick County, Virginia, and died 8 October 1846 in Ripley County, Indiana. He was buried in Napoleon, Ripley County, Indiana, Culver Cemetery.  He married Sarah Presley/Pressley about 1782 in Har
2 CONC rodsburg, Mercer County, Kentucky. She was born 1765 in Virginia and died 1830 in Ripley, Jefferson County, Indiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: 
2 CONT
2 CONT KYNELSON-L Archives--  http://listsearches.rootsweb.com/th/read/KYNELSON/2005-04/1114293526> "Dolores Kennedy" < mythmkr@bellsouth.net>
2 CONT
2 CONT A.R. Ison ,researcher Harrodsburg Historical Society 1987
2 CONT
