1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rev. Peter Tranberg and Rev. Andreas Windrufwa were sent to America from Sweden in 1726 to pastor the Swedish Lutheran Church congregations along the Delaware.  In route they were shipwrecked on the coast of Norway
2 CONC . They continued their journey via Amsterdam and London.
2 CONT
2 CONT New Castle County, Delaware Wills, 1682-1800 about Peter Tranberg
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Peter Tranberg  Will Loc: Will.  Will Made Date: 23 Jan 1744  Will Probate Date: 27 Dec 1748  Will Book: G  Page: 196  Comment: Sister in Sweden, Annika Tranberg; wife, Ann Catharine; eldest son, Andrew Tranberg; daus Rebecc
2 CONC a and Elizabeth Tranberg; son, Peter Tranberg. Exc. Ann Catharine Tranberg, (wife); Andrew Tranberg, (son).
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca married Adolph Benzelstjerna, who met Benjamin Franklin in London
