1 NOTE Peter arrived in America in 1726, and became the pastor of the SwedishLuthern churches in Jew Jersey and at Christina.  He mastered the Englishlanguage and was a popular preacher.  He wrote a letter to thecongregation at Racoon Cr
2 CONC eek in Gloucester, NJ, in 1743 after he had beentransfered to the church at Christina.  He urged the members to apply tothe Bishop in Swedland for a replacement and sugested that he andtheWicacoa minister assist them, along with M
2 CONC r. Brycelius, a Moravianclergyman favored by many members.  Paul Daniel Brycelius. a young Swede,was a graduate of the college at Upsala, Sweden, as was Rev. Tranberg.
