1 NOTE {geni:about_me} I don't have definitive proof that Matthias Richman is the father of Daniel Richman, but the circumstantial evidence is considerable.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Daniel's will, he had a brother named Matthias.
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthias was not a very common name.  There were 7 heads of household named Matthias or Mathias in Salem County, NJ, in the 1830 census (the earliest available federal census for NJ).
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthias the elder's maternal grandfather was named Matthias.
2 CONT
2 CONT Willow Grove was a very small region of Pittsgrove.  Daniel Richman was a miller there.  Buried at the Willow Grove cemetery are several of Matthias the younger's children, and Matthias the elder's wife, and one of the Matthiases.
2 CONT
2 CONT Several unofficial online sites have the two Matthiases as father and son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many sources have this Matthias living 100 years, 1739-1839, but I suspect that they are relying on a will which is likely Matthias, brother of Daniel.  The 1830 census has only one Matthias Richman in New Jersey, and he is 60-70 
2 CONC years old.  The will is that of Matthias Richman of Pittsgrove.  There are no males over 90 in the whole town of Pittsgrove in the 1830 census.  There is no Matthias Richman in the 1840 census, furthering the notion that the 1839 
2 CONC will is that of Matthias Richman, brother of Daniel, born in the 1760s.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.interment.net/data/us/nj/salem/willowgrove/index.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT This has grave inscriptions for many Richman, including:
2 CONT
2 CONT Richman, Hannah, d. 12-21-1875, aged 62y 2m 14d, W/o Mc Kendree Richman
2 CONT
2 CONT Richman, Hannah, d. 8-14-1813, aged 73y 4m 11d, W/o Mathias Richmond
2 CONT
2 CONT Richman, John H., d. 5-22-1871, aged 8y 3m, S/o Mc Kendree & Hannah Richman
2 CONT
