1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to web note on pictures search.ancestry.com, Daniel DuPuy, 1719-1807, was buried in monument and wife Eleanor Cox/Cock DuPuy [it states part of inscription "To the memory of wife Eleanor Cox DuPuy" per Pe
2 CONC digree she died after 1805 and before husband in 1807]. Also, son Daniel DuPuy, Jr. was buried in the DuPuy monument; he died in 1826.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel's parents Jean Du Puy & Anne Chardavoine [born about 1693, died about 1769] married about 1714 Church Du St. Esprit, New York, New York, USA . Daniel married Eleanor [Helena or Elianor Cock] Cox (born 1719, died 1805), on 6
2 CONC  Sep 1746 in Pennsylvania. She is buried in Christ Church under Du Puy or as Dupee in her father Peter Cock/Cox's will of 1748.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks to Kenneth McAlpine, FAG #48356425, for this information.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a partner from 1772 to 1805 with Daniel and John Dupuy in Philadelphia PA as DUPUY & SONS. (silversmiths) see: http://freepages.rootsweb.com/~silversmiths/genealogy/makers/silversmiths/93616.htm 
2 CONT
